Leave the unused uuid dependency out of the FossFLOW backend (UnxWares, not upstream as of v1.0.6).

packages/fossflow-backend declares uuid ^9.0.1 but server.js never imports it: only fossflow-lib uses it, and the
web app build bundles it. Installed with the backend production dependencies, uuid 9.0.1 brings CVE-2026-41907
(GHSA-w5hq-g745-h8pq, medium: v3/v5/v6 write out of bounds into a caller buffer) into the image for nothing. The
lockfile keeps uuid for fossflow-lib, so the web app build does not change.

diff -u a/package-lock.json b/package-lock.json
--- a/package-lock.json
+++ b/package-lock.json
@@ -16482,8 +16482,7 @@
         "cors": "^2.8.6",
         "dotenv": "^17.4.2",
         "express": "^5.2.1",
-        "express-rate-limit": "^8.4.1",
-        "uuid": "^9.0.1"
+        "express-rate-limit": "^8.4.1"
       },
       "devDependencies": {
         "nodemon": "^3.1.14"
diff -u a/packages/fossflow-backend/package.json b/packages/fossflow-backend/package.json
--- a/packages/fossflow-backend/package.json
+++ b/packages/fossflow-backend/package.json
